      "format": "Tier List / Ranking",
      "original_slide_count": 9,
      "final_slide_count": 9,
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_number": 1,
          "slide_label": "Slide 1",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "worst vs best workout splits I've tried"
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 2,
          "slide_label": "Slide 2",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "save this. you'll need it at the gym"
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 3,
          "slide_label": "Slide 3",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "worst: Bro Split. 0/10. you hit each muscle once a week, and that almost never gives you clear growth."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 4,
          "slide_label": "Slide 4",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "PPL and Arnold Split. 5/10. the split trains you 6 days and rests you 1. way too little recovery, especially vs splits that hit muscles twice a week."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 5,
          "slide_label": "Slide 5",
          "is_metafi_slide": true,
          "text": "get a lifting plan that actually adjusts to your week and your goal\ntry the app"
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 6,
          "slide_label": "Slide 6",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "best: Anterior/Posterior. 10/10. hits each muscle twice a week, with at least 3 rest days."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 7,
          "slide_label": "Slide 7",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "and the big one: there's no full leg day to wreck you."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 8,
          "slide_label": "Slide 8",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "Full Body. 8/10. great if you're short on time and can only train 2-3 days a week."
        },
        {
          "slide_number": 9,
          "slide_label": "Slide 9",
          "is_metafi_slide": false,
          "text": "Upper/Lower. 7/10. close to Anterior/Posterior, just with legs on their own day."
        }
      ]
    },
